  "result": "Excellent! All 170 tests pass (146 existing + 24 new payment terms tests).\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n\u2705 **src/errors.js** \u2014 Added new error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID`: Terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n\u2705 **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added payment terms support:\n- `isValidTerms(terms)`: Validates terms are one of NET14, NET30, or EOM\n- `getDueDate(issueDate, terms)`: Calculates due date based on terms:\n  - NET14: 14 days from issue date\n  - NET30: 30 days from issue date\n  - EOM: Last day of the month of issue date\n- Updated `createInvoice()`:\n  - Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on all new invoices\n  - Validates terms and returns TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n  - Preserves terms and dueDate through all invoice operations (addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice)\n\n\u2705 **test/terms.test.js** \u2014 24 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Default NET30 terms\n- NET14, NET30, and EOM term acceptance\n- Invalid terms rejection (unknown terms, case-sensitive validation)\n- Due date calculations for each term type\n- Month/year boundary crossing (NET14/NET30 add days correctly)\n- February leap year edge cases (2024 leap year = Feb 29, 2025 non-leap = Feb 28)\n- EOM calculations for 28, 29, 30, 31-day months\n- Terms and dueDate preservation through addLine, removeLine, issueInvoice\n- Data integrity (no mutation, multiple invoices can have different terms)\n\nAll tests pass with proper UTC date handling and immutable data transformations.",
